From: Thomas <yusenrong46@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:20:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Route indirect first-person risk to support and stop
 clearly past risk locking chat

The English phrase router missed indirect risk ("better off without me", "ending
it all", "suicidal", "won't be around much longer") and sent clearly historical
statements ("I used to want to die but therapy helped") into sticky support mode,
which closes the composer. Indirect phrasings are added; a past marker before a risk
phrase is treated as history only when the same clause has no present marker.
Reported risk about someone else still routes to support. Still not a classifier.

Tests: tests/test_safety_indirect_and_historical.py (17 failed on the previous
router), with replacement known-gap cases. Skill .3 is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
